From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Load URI and Carp for direct URI::Nested consumers

URI::Nested calls URI->new and Carp::croak but does not load either module.
The upstream tests happen to import URI before exercising URI::Nested, so
they pass while a fresh process using URI::Nested directly fails at new().
Load the two already-declared runtime modules explicitly without changing
the public API or URI behavior.

Patch-Source: URI-Nested-0.10 exact source direct-import reproduction
Patch-License: GPL-1.0-or-later OR Artistic-1.0-Perl
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (automated upstream writes forbidden)
Remove-When: Upstream URI::Nested loads URI and Carp itself.
---
diff --git a/lib/URI/Nested.pm b/lib/URI/Nested.pm
--- a/lib/URI/Nested.pm
+++ b/lib/URI/Nested.pm
@@ -3,4 +3,6 @@
 use strict;
+use URI;
+use Carp;
 use 5.8.1;
 our $VERSION = '0.10';
 use overload '""' => 'as_string', fallback => 1;
